THE ECHO OF A FISH - (15s · 30fps · 9:16 · high-definition)

STYLE & LOOK

Hyper-detailed translucent red fish skeleton drifting through a pale, misty void.
Every movement produces a soft, semi-transparent trail — like red ink dissolving in water or smoke ribbons drifting behind it.
The skeleton has dreamlike swimming behavior, smooth and fluid.

GLOBAL MOTION RULES (UPGRADED FOR FISH MOVEMENT)

The fish swims with subtle body undulation — smooth S-curve motion.
Every motion leaves a smoky red trail (not thick, not gore — artistic ink diffusion).
Trails slowly break apart into wispy threads.
Fins move in delicate, fan-like pulses.
The fish never stops moving; even at slow moments, it glides.
Camera always moves slightly: arc, drift, macro passes.

13-SCENE SCRIPT (now with full swimming + ink trails)
Scene 1 (0.0–1.1s) — FIRST GLIDE

Macro on the skull as the fish begins a gentle forward glide.
A thin ink-thread flows from behind the head, dispersing softly.

Scene 2 (1.1–2.2s) — THE UNDULATION

Camera widens as the fish body undulates left–right in a slow S-motion.
The spine leaves a curved smoky trail, lingering behind.

Scene 3 (2.2–3.3s) — FIN BLOOM

Fins flutter like translucent fans.
Each flap releases tiny wisp clouds of red ink drifting outward.

Scene 4 (3.3–4.4s) — SPIRAL TURN

The fish turns upward in a spiral.
The trail forms a helix of red smoke that slowly unravels.

Scene 5 (4.4–5.5s) — CAMERA DIVE UNDER

Camera slides underneath as the fish swims overhead.
Ink trails drift downward like falling ribbons.

Scene 6 (5.5–6.6s) — MOMENTARY STILLNESS

The fish slows, hovering.
Ink behind it swirls gently, forming soft red clouds, then dispersing.

Scene 7 (6.6–7.7s) — ACCELERATION

Sudden graceful thrust — tail flicks.
A long comet-like ink tail stretches behind as it surges forward.

Scene 8 (7.7–8.8s) — DRIFT AND FADE

The fish pauses mid-swim; previous smoke trails drift behind it in layered parallax.
Camera drifts through one of the smoke ribbons.

Scene 9 (8.8–9.9s) — INK VORTEX

As it turns sharply, the trail forms a small vortex of red wisps around its spine.

Scene 10 (9.9–11.0s) — FULL BODY SWIM

Wide shot: the fish swims in a gentle arc across the frame, leaving a wide ink cloud shaped like a brushstroke.

Scene 11 (11.0–12.1s) — THE MEMORY PATH

Old trails linger in the background while new ones form.
Camera tracks the skeleton as it glides through its own fading echoes.

Scene 12 (12.1–13.2s) — LIFT INTO LIGHT

The fish swims upward, trails drifting downward like dissolving watercolor.

Scene 13 (13.2–14.6s) — DISAPPEARING CURRENTS
The fish makes one final graceful swim left-to-right, leaving its brightest trail yet.
The trail spreads, thins, and fades into white haze.

